From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:01:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] HID: ithc: Match feature responses to the requested report ID

The driver completes a pending GET_FEATURE request with whatever
feature response arrives next, and passes a feature response that
nobody is waiting for to hid_input_report().

The touch controller of the Surface Pro 9 (045E:0C52, legacy mode)
answers a GET_FEATURE for report 17 with two responses: the 64-byte
report, immediately followed by a second response that contains only
the report ID. Of the ten feature reports read on this device (5, 6,
9, 17, 35, 72, 86, 102, 112, 115) only report 17 does this, on every
request. Why the firmware sends the second response is not known.

Depending on when the next request is made, the extra response either
arrives with no request pending and is rejected by the HID core,

  hid-generic 0001:045E:0C52.0001: Event data for report 17 was too short (63 vs 0)
  ithc 0000:00:10.6: ithc_hid_process_data: hid_input_report failed with -22

or it completes the next request, so that e.g. HIDIOCGFEATURE for
report 112 returns the single byte 0x11 instead of the report, without
any error.

Both the legacy and the HIDSPI decoders hand over feature responses
with the report ID in the first byte. Remember the ID of the pending
request and complete the request only with a response that starts with
that ID. Requests for report ID 0 (devices without report IDs) accept
any response as before.

Drop responses that do not match instead of passing them to
hid_input_report(). No request is waiting for them, and a response that
is long enough to be accepted there would be delivered to hidraw
readers such as iptsd as if it were an input report.

A request for the same report made right after the first one can still
be completed by the extra response; it then returns one byte, which
the caller can tell from the length.

Signed-off-by: Joonhoe Kim <26rote@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.c | 18 ++++++++++++++----
 drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 15 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.c b/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.c
index 065646ab4..edc2a7cfa 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.c
+++ b/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.c
@@ -59,6 +59,7 @@ static int ithc_hid_raw_request(struct hid_device *hdev, unsigned char reportnum
 		// Prepare for response.
 		mutex_lock(&ithc->hid.get_feature_mutex);
 		ithc->hid.get_feature_buf = buf;
+		ithc->hid.get_feature_id = reportnum;
 		ithc->hid.get_feature_size = len;
 		mutex_unlock(&ithc->hid.get_feature_mutex);
 
@@ -132,9 +133,16 @@ void ithc_hid_process_data(struct ithc *ithc, struct ithc_data *d)
 	case ITHC_DATA_GET_FEATURE:
 	{
 		// Response to a 'get feature' request sent by ithc_hid_raw_request().
+		// The data starts with the report ID. Only a response for the report that is
+		// being waited for completes the request: devices can send more than one
+		// response per request (the SP9 touch controller follows the response for
+		// report 17 with a second one containing only the ID), and the extra one
+		// would otherwise be returned as the data of the next request.
+		// (Report ID 0 means the device doesn't use report IDs, so we can't check.)
 		bool done = false;
 		mutex_lock(&ithc->hid.get_feature_mutex);
-		if (ithc->hid.get_feature_buf) {
+		if (ithc->hid.get_feature_buf && (!ithc->hid.get_feature_id ||
+				(d->size && *(u8 *)d->data == ithc->hid.get_feature_id))) {
 			if (d->size < ithc->hid.get_feature_size)
 				ithc->hid.get_feature_size = d->size;
 			memcpy(ithc->hid.get_feature_buf, d->data, ithc->hid.get_feature_size);
@@ -146,9 +154,11 @@ void ithc_hid_process_data(struct ithc *ithc, struct ithc_data *d)
 			wake_up(&ithc->hid.wait_get_feature);
 		} else {
 			// Received data without a matching request, or the request already
-			// timed out. (XXX What's the correct thing to do here?)
-			CHECK(hid_input_report, ithc->hid.dev, HID_FEATURE_REPORT,
-				NOCONST(d->data), d->size, 1);
+			// timed out. Drop it: nobody is waiting for it, and passing it to
+			// hid_input_report() would deliver it to hidraw readers as if it were
+			// an input report (or fail with -EINVAL if it is shorter than the report).
+			pci_dbg(ithc->pci, "dropped unexpected feature response (size %u, report ID 0x%02x)\n",
+				d->size, d->size ? *(u8 *)d->data : 0);
 		}
 		return;
 	}
diff --git a/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.h b/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.h
index 599eb912c..0b8d4a943 100644
--- a/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.h
+++ b/drivers/hid/ithc/ithc-hid.h
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ struct ithc_hid {
 	wait_queue_head_t wait_get_feature;
 	struct mutex get_feature_mutex;
 	void *get_feature_buf;
+	u8 get_feature_id;
 	size_t get_feature_size;
 };
 
